module gunbc.bare_reference_scanner_admission

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import std.disposition { Disposition, Terminal }
import std.types { String }
import v2.std.collection { List }

data bare_reference_scanner_admission_authority_disposition: Disposition = Terminal {
  reason: "Single authority for the SEED-GROWTH RECEIPT owed by the bare-reference scanner change (gunbc#9102). It declares WHICH hand-authored Rust declarations that change adds to the seed, why they are there, and what retires them. It does NOT admit them: the realization disposition for the scanner itself is an operator judgment (ScaffoldAdmitted / TerminalOrRetainedKernel / RejectedForFinalConstruction) and is deliberately NOT asserted here. A receipt that also granted its own admission would be the self-authorized dissolution failure DESIGN names — an author who can write a scaffold can equally write a row claiming it was approved. The row is Terminal because the RECEIPT is permanent: it survives the scanner it describes, recording what was owed and on what trigger it was discharged."
}

data bare_reference_scanner_presumption_note: String = "THE SCAFFOLD PRESUMPTION STANDS AND IS NOT ARGUED AWAY HERE. module_self_declared_names re-parses language structure from raw source text; the facts it reconstructs — declarations, coproduct variants, type parameters, lambda binders — belong to parsing or ingestion, which already own them; and it sits in cli_run.rs. None of those three grounds scales with size, so the measured 115 lines (116 by the census's inclusive span, which counts the signature line) rather than a circulated ~603 changes HOW MUCH debt is on the table, never WHETHER the presumption applies. A 115-line raw-text scanner re-derives the same parser-owned facts as a 603-line one.\n\nWHAT THE CORRECT FIGURE DOES CHANGE: the operator is being asked to dispose of ONE production item of 115 lines, not nine items of 603.\n\nWHY THE SCANNER EXISTS AT ALL, stated as the cost of NOT having it rather than as a justification: the bare-reference census resolves a name against the whole pool. Without knowing which names a module BINDS or DECLARES, a lambda parameter, a type parameter and a module's own coproduct variant are each scanned as references out and pulled a module that happened to declare that spelling. Measured on the import-free corpus: 172 sources / 65 blocking without the guards, 94 / 2 with them, main byte-identical at 99 / 0 in every arm.\n\nTHE TERMINAL CONSTRUCTION IS NOT THIS. It is the parse phase publishing the binder and declaration facts it already computes, so no consumer re-derives them from text. Until that surface exists the scanner is the only thing standing between an import-free corpus and a whole-pool over-pull, and that is an argument for a bounded exception, never for keeping it."

data bare_reference_scanner_not_growth_note: String = "WHAT IS NOT GROWTH AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED, so a modification is never netted into an addition census. THREE existing items are MODIFIED rather than added — bare_identifier_candidates (a new arm inside its existing scan loop), bare_reference_pull_paths_for_source (two new skip conditions in its existing resolve loop, plus provenance carried on the existing trace line), and project_roadmap_acceptance_event_history_from_authority_text_builtin. Their disposition is ExistingSeedItemModified. Listing them above would inflate the addition count by three and understate nothing, which is exactly the direction that makes a census look conservative while being wrong.\n\nTHE AUTHORITATIVE G0 CENSUS OVER-REPORTS THIS DIFF BY 100 PERCENT, AND THE RECONCILIATION IS STATED HERE SO THE NEXT AUTHOR DOES NOT CONCLUDE THIS RECEIPT IS WRONG. scripts/rust_item_census.py --diff origin/main reports EIGHTEEN added hand items. NINE are the real declarations enumerated above. The other NINE are fixture .dag source authored inside Rust raw string literals as test input — type VisibilityScope, type FrameExtent, type CostBasis, type CostAccount, type Result, fn trim_one, type Dimension, type Scale, fn g. They are data, not declarations, and counting them is the same shape as counting a script's own echo as its output.\n\nTHE DENOMINATORS ARE DIFFERENT AND MUST BE NAMED, because three plausible counts circulate. EIGHTEEN is the census ITEM total. NINE is the deduplicated phantom ITEM count. TWELVE is the count of fixture LINES in the diff, which is larger because CostAccount is authored twice (bare and parameterized) and fn f is authored twice (over List<Int> and List<Row>) — the census enrols an item once and the line scan sees each spelling. A reader who adds an item count to a line count gets a number that reconciles with nothing.\n\nTHE CENSUS DEFECT IS PREDICTED BY THE CENSUS ITSELF: gunbc.seed_growth_admission seed_growth_g0_census_host_scaffold_note records that its item extraction is regex, parallel to but outside the dag/extdeps/languages/ rust grammar authority. This is that prediction firing. It is also the exact class of the artifact this receipt admits — a raw-text recognizer miscounting language structure because it reads source as text rather than consulting the authority that owns the structure — which is the strongest available argument that the terminal construction named in bare_reference_scanner_presumption_note is the right one for both."

data bare_reference_scanner_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run",
      decl_name: "module_self_declared_names",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run",
      decl_name: "bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "self_declared_names_collect_every_coproduct_form",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "blank_lines_do_not_end_a_coproduct_block",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "an_alias_target_is_a_reference_out_not_a_declared_variant",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "a_single_variant_coproduct_with_a_payload_is_still_a_declaration",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "record_field_labels_are_not_self_declared",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "bare_arrow_lambda_parameter_is_bound_but_a_match_arm_head_is_not",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.bare_reference_scanner_tests",
      decl_name: "named_argument_and_comma_positioned_lambdas_bind_too",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST IS STILL NEEDED HERE: the bare-reference census runs inside the seed's own source loader, deciding which files enter a closure BEFORE any parse result exists to consult. It cannot read a parse-phase binder surface that the closure it is constructing has not yet produced. That is a bootstrap ordering constraint, not seed-shrink debt.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE — does the change serve the v2 self-host program. An import-free corpus is the namespace cut, and without these guards the cut's regen subject refuses with roughly 65 hard diagnostics. This is defect repair on the self-host path.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA, AND IT IS TWO NUMBERS AGAINST TWO BASES BECAUSE THEY ANSWER TWO QUESTIONS. From the merge base bd84f6696 the delta is +9 — ONE production item (module_self_declared_names) and EIGHT test scaffolding items (the module plus seven test fns) — and that is the AUTHORSHIP question: what did this branch write. Against current main (fd55f00bc6 onward) the delta is +8, ALL test scaffolding and ZERO production items, and that is the SEED-GROWTH question: what does merging this add to the seed. The second number is the one this receipt exists to answer.\n\nWHY THEY DIFFER: gunbc#9090 landed a BYTE-IDENTICAL copy of module_self_declared_names on main while this PR was open — verified absent at the merge base, present on main, and md5-identical to the copy here, so the two are the same function and not merely similar. Git collapses identical additions at one location, so the merge produces exactly one definition with zero conflict markers: nothing breaks mechanically, which is precisely why no reviewer, no gate and neither author noticed.\n\nTHE CONSEQUENCE FOR THE DISPOSITION, STATED SO IT IS NOT DECIDED IN IGNORANCE: the main copy carries NO seed-growth receipt — nothing in any .dag on main names module_self_declared_names — so a 115-line hand-written source scanner is already in the frozen v1 seed unadmitted, and the only receipt that would admit it is this one, behind this PR. A RejectedForFinalConstruction verdict therefore no longer removes the scanner from the seed; it removes the receipt and leaves the unadmitted copy standing. The operator is disposing of a function that is already there, and refusal does not restore the prior state.\n\nWHAT THIS IS NOT: an accusation. Two sessions independently needed the same fact — which names a module declares — and independently wrote the same scanner. That is the terminal construction argument made by the corpus rather than by an author: when the parse phase does not publish a fact, the number of hand re-derivations is bounded only by the number of consumers who need it. THREE existing items are modified and are listed in bare_reference_scanner_not_growth_note instead, never netted in here.\n\nHAND-LOC DELTA: +413 / -17 against origin/main, entirely in src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs. NO OTHER .rs FILE CHANGES ON THIS BRANCH AT ALL, and the way that sentence was got wrong once is worth more than the sentence. Measured from the MERGE BASE (git diff bd84f66..HEAD), the branch touches exactly three files: this module, the roster row, and cli_run.rs. An earlier revision of this row named five generated mirrors as having moved on the branch. They had not. That reading came from diffing against origin/main, which puts main on the LEFT, so main's own commits since the branch point rendered as deletions authored here — the branch was behind main, not editing mirrors. The receipt then carried a false population, and a second session independently verified the generated-file exemption for five files this branch never touched: a correct verification of an invented premise, which is the failure mode where two parties agree and both are wrong. The rule this row now stands on: a branch delta is measured from the MERGE BASE, never from the moving tip, and a hand-LOC census that names a file must be reproducible by a command that states its base. A large share is the doc comments carrying the receipts for each guard and the census of the arm the shape rule cannot decide.\n\nWHAT THIS RECEIPT DOES NOT DO: it does not admit the scanner. The realization disposition is an operator judgment and fails closed in its absence — see bare_reference_scanner_admission_authority_disposition.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all nine declarations when the parse phase publishes the binder and declaration facts this scanner re-derives from text — module-local declaration names, coproduct variant heads, declaration type parameters, and lambda binder names — so the source loader consults a parse-owned surface instead of scanning source. That is the same terminal construction bare_reference_scanner_presumption_note names, and it retires the scanner whole rather than shrinking it.",
  current_boundary: "gunbc.bare_reference_scanner_admission -> v1_compiler.cli_run module_self_declared_names -> v1_compiler.cli_run bare_reference_pull_paths_for_source -> the both-closure edge index"
}
